Problem statement
Analysts working with enterprise systems (SAP, Oracle, Salesforce) waste significant time finding the right data:
Scale & Complexity: Systems like SAP have thousands of cryptically-named tables (BSEG, EKKO, VBAP). Even a simple invoice process can span 10-15 tables.
Customization Challenges: Companies add custom fields, Z-tables, and modified workflows — standard documentation doesn't match reality.
Knowledge Silos: Only a few busy experts know which tables to use and what fields mean. When they're unavailable or leave the company, their knowledge disappears with them.
Productivity Loss: Analysts spend 30-50% of early project time searching docs, testing queries, and waiting for expert answers.
Target audience = Potential users & Beneficiaries
Data Engineers & Developers - building data pipelines and analytics solutions.
Analytics Consultants - designing process mining and BI solutions (e.g., Celonis implementations).
Project Managers - requiring quick scoping and estimation information.
Business Stakeholders - seeking clarity on data availability and use case feasibility
Business impact 
Find the right data in minutes, not hours or days
Stop waiting for busy system experts – let them focus on complex problems
Finish discovery and design phases 20-40% faster
Minimize errors from incorrect table/field usage
Get new team members up to speed quickly
Build a knowledge base you can reuse on future projects
Approach to solution
Architecture v0
AI Assistant (Librarian) — user interface in MS Teams. Users ask natural questions in chat: "Which table contains payment terms?" or "List tables for invoice analysis".
Agent built with MS Copilot Studio + MS Power Automate.
Knowledge Repository (Vector Database ChromaDB) — runs locally, stores and searches across all three sources simultaneously:
Prebuilt Knowledge — standard system data model documentation, created using Celonis AP app.
Client System Metadata — data structures extracted from the client's system (e.g., DD03M table in SAP).
Client Technical Documentation — PDF files uploaded to the database.
MVP focuses on SAP Accounts Payable process; future phases expand to other modules and systems.
